# Figure 1 legend
R("Figure 1. a) Schematic representation of the MDFS framework",
  "b) Information gain in the 2D mode identified by MDFS-2D across taxa, functions, and their combination. Each point represents a feature, with its position reflecting its 2D IG (y-axis) against the IG in 1D (x-axis), calculated as the mean across leave-one-cohort-out cross-validation folds and repeated MDFS runs on the pooled training set within each fold. Points above the diagonal indicate synergy - those whose 2D IG exceeds the 1D IG. Among the significant features considered in this analysis (top 2% of pairs by total IG in each MDFS run, retained if selected in >=6 of 10 runs), all passed the synergy criteria (2D IG > 1D IG).",
  f"b) Joint 2D information gain of every directed feature pair (base feature, contributing feature) evaluated by MDFS-2D in the taxonomic ({fmt(N['fig1b']['taxa']['directed_pairs'])} pairs), functional ({fmt(N['fig1b']['functions']['directed_pairs'])}) and combined ({fmt(N['fig1b']['combined']['directed_pairs'])}) feature spaces. x-axis: 1D IG of the base feature; y-axis: 1D IG of the base feature plus the IG added by the contributing feature, both averaged over the leave-one-cohort-out folds and MDFS runs (14 × 10) in which both features were present. Grey: pairs that never passed the pair-level significance threshold; coloured: pairs that passed the significance and synergy filters, coloured by the percentage of fold-run combinations in which they did. Points on the diagonal carry no 2D gain; the pairs retained for synthetic-feature construction (top 2% by joint IG in >= 6 of 10 runs) lie far above it.",
  "Reviewer 2, comment 8 (and the all-pairs version of the figure): the panel now shows every evaluated pair, not only the selected ones, so the reader sees how the retained pairs relate to the full search space. Points are pairs, not features. Produced by R1_synergistic_pairs/figure1b_all_pairs/ (manuscript/Figure1b.png).")

